// Jobs.
//
// Every job has a giver now, and a mark over their head while they have one
// to hand out or to pay for (HubScreen.drawQuestMarks). The givers are the
// villagers' roles: `guide` is Ốc, `guard` Tôm, `trader` Cam, `explorer` Mực.
// A giver offers the first of theirs that is open, in id order, so a giver's
// jobs that must come in an order say so with `requires`.
//
// THE NEWCOMER'S ROUND. Ốc's nine, one after another: the island's every
// trade, each paying what the next one wants - the wood for the first meal, the
// seeds for the field, the shards for the forge - with gold and a stone, and the
// thing the job was about. He walks the player to each (quest.Places).
//
// THE TUTORIAL. `first_blood`, `the_herbalists_errand`, `down_the_well` and
// `the_masters_lesson`, Tôm, Cam, Mực and Tôm again: that monsters drop
// things, that the village buys them, that the stairs go down. Two ids still
// name who gave them before - an id is what a profile saves a job under.
//
// THE LOST NINJAS. Tôm pulled the ninjas out of the surf; the five he did not
// find are out there still. Each `rescue_` brings one home (rewardCharacter),
// one after another once his lesson is done. The stall still sells them.
//
// THE DUNGEON'S WORK. The bounties that used to hang with nobody to hand them
// over, each now somebody's, paying gear and a weapon for the main hand or the
// off hand. `three_counts` repeats: the Dead Land's three vampires, again and
// again, for gold and stones and a chance at a heavy weapon - three in ten - and
// one in twenty at the anchor, the hardest-hitting blow there is.
//
// Steps name things that already exist and are checked against them at boot
// (notes/d.md, "Quest step kinds"); `any` meets every target of its kind.
